  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A nonuniform rod&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mi>O</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow> </math> &nbsp;of length&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></math>&nbsp;has linear mass density that varies with the distance&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;from left end of the rod according to&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub> <mi>λ</mi> <mn>0</mn> </msub> <mfenced> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <msup> <mi>x</mi> <mn>3</mn> </msup> </mrow> <mrow> <msup> <mi>L</mi> <mn>3</mn> </msup> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </mfenced></mrow> </math>; Where&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <msub> <mi>λ</mi> <mn>0</mn> </msub> </mrow> </math> &nbsp;is constant, is kept&nbsp;along&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis&nbsp;and is rotating about an axis&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow> </math>, which is perpendicular to the rod as&nbsp;shown in the figure. What is the value of <math> <mi>x</mi> </math> &nbsp;so that moment of inertia of&nbsp;rod about axis&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mi>A</mi><mi>B&nbsp;</mi><mfenced> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>I</mtext> <mrow> <mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow> </msub> </mrow> </mfenced></mrow> </math> &nbsp;is minimum?</p>\r\r<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0111_aefc84f4f230.jpg\" style=\"width: 362px; height: 232px;\" /></p>\r\r<p>&nbsp;</p>\r"
